{# Home-page hero (architecture.md Phase 14): full-bleed cover photo behind the transparent
   site header (see .has-hero in header.css/base.njk) and the heading/tagline/intro, styled
   after a reference "cover-photo hero" layout the user shared — full-width image, header
   floating over its top portion, heading/subscribe-style content lower in the frame.
   .hero__media--placeholder is a gradient stand-in until a real photo is chosen — see
   ROADMAP_TODO.md Phase 14's open "own vs. KTO-sourced" + cover/contain decisions. Swap to a
   real <img> (or background-image) inside .hero__media without touching anything else here. #}
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
  <div class="hero__media hero__media--placeholder" data-hero-media aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="hero__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="hero__content">
    <h1 id="hero-heading" class="hero__heading">{{ site.name }}</h1>
    <p class="hero__tagline">{{ site.tagline }}</p>
    <p class="hero__intro">
      Korea's F-1-D Digital Nomad Visa lets you live and work remotely from Korea for up to
      three years — but the income bar is lower, and life is better, outside the Seoul capital
      area. Find out which regions you qualify for, then see what a month-long stay actually
      looks like there.
    </p>

    {# Calculator mount point (ROADMAP Phase 16 target: real <form>, salary/age/family inputs,
       calls eligibility.js, renders the caption below into #eligibility-result, writes
       sessionStorage). Empty on purpose — this is the mount point, not the implementation, so
       nothing renders here yet. #}
    <div id="calculator" class="calculator-mount" data-calculator-mount>
      <noscript>
        <p class="calculator-mount__noscript">
          The eligibility calculator needs JavaScript. See the
          <a href="/visa-info/">visa income thresholds</a> directly instead.
        </p>
      </noscript>
    </div>

    {# Result-caption mount point — calculator.js (Phase 16) owns all caption rendering here;
       korea-map.js (Phase 17) only applies map state, it doesn't touch this element. #}
    <p
      id="eligibility-result"
      class="eligibility-result"
      data-eligibility-result
      aria-live="polite"
      hidden
    ></p>
  </div>
</section>
